<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">2 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 2 April, from 742 to 2005.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charlemagne.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">742 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,284 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charlemagne is born, by tradition on this day</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>, future King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a> and emperor in the West, was traditionally born on 2 April; the year may have been as late as 748. His empire united much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-europe">Western Europe</a> for the first time since <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-europe">Western Europe</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1513">1513 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">513 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ponce de León sights the coast he names La Florida</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Spanish explorer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-ponce-de-leon">Juan Ponce de León</a> sighted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> coast during the Easter season, Pascua Florida, which gave the land its name. His was the first recorded European landing in what is now the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1792">1792 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">234 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US Coinage Act creates the dollar and the Mint</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Congress passed the Coinage Act, establishing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Mint in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philadelphia">Philadelphia</a> and defining the dollar in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> and gold. It laid the foundations of American currency.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1865">1865 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">161 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jefferson Davis abandons Richmond as Petersburg falls</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">As Union troops broke through the Petersburg lines, Confederate President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jefferson-davis">Jefferson Davis</a> and his government fled Richmond by train. Lee surrendered at Appomattox a week later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1982">1982 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">44 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Argentina invades the Falkland Islands</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Argentine forces seized the British-held Falklands, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a> claims as the Malvinas. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> sent a naval task force; the ten-week war ended in Argentine surrender and hastened the fall of the junta.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2005">2005 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">21 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope John Paul II dies after a 26-year pontificate</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">John Paul II, the first non-Italian pope in over four centuries, died in the Vatican. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a>, one of the longest in history, was closely tied to the fall of communism in his native <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>.</p></div></li></ol>
